6 +17,49 @@"," "," namespace duckdb {"," ","+class TaskExecutor;","+class TaskExecutorTask;","+","+//! A unit of work scheduled on a TaskExecutor","+//! Deliberately not a Task: it cannot be handed to the TaskScheduler directly, it cannot be descheduled or","+//! rescheduled, and it cannot report partial progress. The executor wraps it and owns cancellation, error handling","+//! and task accounting, so implementations only have to describe their work.","+class BaseExecutorTask {","+public:","+\texplicit BaseExecutorTask(TaskExecutor &executor);","+\tvirtual ~BaseExecutorTask() = default;","+","+public:","+\t//! Perform the task's work in one call - throwing is allowed, the executor captures the error and cancels the","+\t//! other tasks. Run-to-completion tasks override this.","+\tvirtual void ExecuteTask() {","+\t\tthrow InternalException(\"BaseExecutorTask::ExecuteTask was not implemented\");","+\t}","+\t//! Perform one unit of work, returning TASK_NOT_FINISHED while more remains and TASK_FINISHED when done.","+\t//! Incremental tasks override this instead of ExecuteTask; the default runs the whole task in one call. The","+\t//! executor loops this to completion while draining, and calls it once per turn on a background thread so the","+\t//! task yields cooperatively. The mode never reaches the task: the wrapper owns the loop.","+\tvirtual TaskExecutionResult ExecuteTaskStep() {","+\t\tExecuteTask();","+\t\treturn TaskExecutionResult::TASK_FINISHED;","+\t}","+\t//! Called instead of ExecuteTask when the task is retired without running its work, because another task errored,","+\t//! because the executor was cancelled, or because the task could not be queued at all. Exactly one of ExecuteTask","+\t//! or Cancel runs for every task passed to TaskExecutor::ScheduleTask.","+\t//! Anything a waiter watches must change on every exit path, or that waiter never wakes up. Either settle it here","+\t//! as well as in ExecuteTask, or settle it in the destructor, which also